---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const deeper = [
  {
    title: 'Explore the research record',
    copy: 'Browse notes, drafts, results and earlier research directions.',
    href: '/explore/',
    label: 'Explore',
  },
  {
    title: 'Methods',
    copy: 'See how studies are designed and how evidence is checked.',
    href: '/method/',
    label: 'Methods',
  },
  {
    title: 'Prior work and lineage',
    copy: 'See the ideas and research this work builds on, including concepts that were narrowed or renamed.',
    href: '/lineage/',
    label: 'Lineage',
  },
  {
    title: 'Provenance',
    copy: 'Inspect contribution history and machine-readable research records.',
    href: '/provenance/',
    label: 'Provenance',
  },
];
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About Agalmic Research, an open research effort studying how abundant knowledge and AI capability can become useful human capability."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Research into what abundance makes possible, and what it makes scarce.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Agalmic Research is an independent, open research effort focused on a simple problem: producing more information and more ideas is becoming easier, but turning them into understanding, good decisions and useful capability is still hard.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
        <h2>Abundance changes the bottleneck.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">When one thing becomes cheap, something else often becomes the limiting factor.</p>
        <p>AI can make writing, searching, coding and idea generation dramatically cheaper. That can make attention, judgment, validation, expertise, trust, energy or implementation more important than before.</p>
        <p>Agalmic Research studies those shifts and looks for ways to turn new abundance into practical gains rather than simply producing more output.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What counts as progress</p>
        <h2>Useful understanding matters more than owning an idea.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Much of the best work starts with knowledge that already exists. Finding a mature theory, a useful dataset, a reliable method or good open-source software can save more effort than inventing a new name for the same problem.</p>
        <p>Progress can take many forms: a clearer explanation, a negative result, a useful experiment, better software, a reusable dataset, a stronger method or a question that has finally become answerable.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="/research/">Research</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/projects/">Projects</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/publications/">Publications</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Under the hood</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>For readers who want more detail.</h2>
          <p>The deeper research machinery is still public, but it is secondary to the ideas and results.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="about-grid">
        {deeper.map((item) => (
          <article class="about-card">
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.copy}</p>
            <a href={item.href}>{item.label} →</a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Open source</p>
        <h2>The work is inspectable.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The website source, research records, literature reviews and supporting code are public where privacy, security or other legitimate constraints do not require otherwise.</p>
        <p>Reusable tools should be easy for others to take and adapt. The site's <strong>astro-agalmic</strong> integration is published under the 0BSD licence.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://github.com/TsatsuAmable/agalmicresearch">GitHub source ↗</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/tools/astro-agalmic/">astro-agalmic</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
